// TEST: Two generic variables mixed by arithmetic refuse two different argument types (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999 @ 9:16
// ERROR-CONTAINS: argument 1 makes it Int64 while argument 2 makes it Float64
// ============================================================================
// `x + y` makes `T` and `U` one variable (functions/264), so an Int64 and a
// Float64 argument disagree about it: the Int64 sum would truncate the 2.5.
// Convert one: `add(Float64(n), 2.5)`.
function add(x: T, y: U) = x + y
let n = 1
let s = add(n, 2.5)
